      "id": "K3.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Provisional contract: POST /events accepts application/json {\"seats\": positive integer} and returns {\"event_id\": string}; POST /events/{event_id}/reservations accepts an empty JSON object and returns {\"reservation_id\": string, \"event_id\": string}. Each reservation takes one seat. Generated IDs are UUID strings. Errors return {\"error\": string}. The launch command and file names remain for discovery or implementation to establish."
    },
    {
      "id": "K3.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Both successful POSTs return 201. Invalid JSON or fields return 400; an unknown path or event returns 404; an unsupported method returns 405; a full event returns 409; an unsupported content type returns 415; and an unexpected server failure returns 500 with a generic error."
    },
    {
      "id": "K4.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "An event has a positive integer capacity. Each accepted reservation consumes exactly one seat; reservations cannot exceed capacity, including under concurrent requests. Capacity remains allocated until the stored data is removed; cancellation is out of scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "K4.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Malformed JSON, missing or extra fields, non-integer or boolean seat counts, seat counts below one, and reservation bodies other than an empty object are invalid. Unknown event IDs are not reservable."
    },
    {
      "id": "K5.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "The service owns event capacities and reservation records in a local SQLite database. They persist across restarts until an operator removes the database. Clients retain returned IDs; no personal identity data is required."
    },
    {
      "id": "K5.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Clients receive IDs in their own responses; there is no listing or read endpoint. The operator can access the database. No authentication or confidentiality between clients is assumed. A transaction must prevent concurrent reservations from exceeding capacity, and committed records survive restart."
    },
    {
      "id": "K6.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Use Python 3.11 or later; discovery should check the available runtime before implementation."
    },
    {
      "id": "K6.2",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Use the Python standard library, including SQLite and unittest; add no third-party dependencies unless discovery establishes a need."
    },
    {
      "id": "K6.3",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Default to listening on 127.0.0.1:8000 with a local SQLite database; the database path and listen address must be configurable. Exact configuration names and deployment values remain to be established."
    },
    {
      "id": "K7.1",
      "basis": "default",
      "answer": "Keep HTTP parsing and responses, reservation rules, and transactional persistence separable so each can be tested and changed independently."
